# A Self-Hosted iCloud Alternative

> A self-hosted cloud dashboard for browsing, downloading, converting, and
> synchronizing files across devices with Syncthing, Flask, Raspberry Pi, and
> Tailscale.

This project is a Python and Flask web application that provides a browser-based
dashboard for files stored in a Syncthing shared folder.

It supports browsing files, downloading files, converting supported formats,
synchronizing with a Raspberry Pi, and securely accessing the dashboard from
trusted devices through Tailscale HTTPS.

## Why I Built It

I wanted to learn how cloud-storage systems work by building a self-hosted
alternative from smaller pieces instead of only using third-party services.

This project combines:

- A Flask web dashboard
- Syncthing device-to-device file synchronization
- A Raspberry Pi storage or synchronization node
- File conversion tools
- Tailscale networking for secure HTTPS remote access
- Security checks for downloads and file conversions

## Features

- Password-protected Flask dashboard
- Browse files in a configured Syncthing shared folder
- Download synchronized files from the browser
- Convert supported document, image, audio, and video formats
- Synchronize files between a Windows computer and Raspberry Pi with Syncthing
- Access the dashboard remotely over HTTPS using Tailscale Serve
- Store local passwords, API keys, and configuration in `.env`
- Use Flask-WTF CSRF protection for forms
- Validate paths in download and conversion routes
- Block `../` path-traversal attempts outside the configured storage folder

